<title>MALAYSIA: Malaysia April 1-20 palm oil exports 429,661t - SGS.</title>
<headline>Malaysia April 1-20 palm oil exports 429,661t - SGS.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cargo surveyor Societe Generale de Surveillance (SGS) Malaysia Sdn Bhd said on Monday it estimated Malaysia's palm oil exports for April 1-20 at 429,661 tonnes against 391,599 tonnes in March 1-20.</p>
<p>It said the exports comprised 128,224 tonnes of RBD palm oil, 165,642 tonnes of RBD palm olein and 38,050 tonnes of RBD palm stearin. The other products totalled 97,745 tonnes.  </p>
<p>Pakistan was the top buyer during the period, taking 71,050 tonnes, followed by China which bought 63,676 tonnes, India (53,555 tonnes), Turkey (25,100 tonnes) and Japan (20,400 tonnes).</p>
<p>Countries in the European Union bought 61,712 tonnes.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-230-7510)</p>
